ength":16},{"pos":4116,"endPos":4130,"startLine":92,"startLineOffset":24,"endLine":92,"endLineOffset":38,"length":15},{"pos":4178,"endPos":4193,"startLine":93,"startLineOffset":36,"endLine":93,"endLineOffset":51,"length":16},{"pos":4200,"endPos":4205,"startLine":93,"startLineOffset":58,"endLine":93,"endLineOffset":63,"length":6},{"pos":4308,"endPos":4322,"startLine":95,"startLineOffset":28,"endLine":95,"endLineOffset":42,"length":15},{"pos":4458,"endPos":4473,"startLine":97,"startLineOffset":28,"endLine":97,"endLineOffset":43,"length":16},{"pos":4561,"endPos":4582,"startLine":99,"startLineOffset":41,"endLine":99,"endLineOffset":62,"length":22},{"pos":4658,"endPos":4712,"startLine":102,"startLineOffset":20,"endLine":102,"endLineOffset":74,"length":55},{"pos":4733,"endPos":5528,"startLine":103,"startLineOffset":20,"endLine":115,"endLineOffset":21,"length":796},{"pos":5580,"endPos":5595,"startLine":119,"startLineOffset":16,"endLine":119,"endLineOffset":31,"length":16},{"pos":5878,"endPos":6035,"startLine":129,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":130,"endLineOffset":43,"length":158},{"pos":6140,"endPos":6159,"startLine":131,"startLineOffset":104,"endLine":131,"endLineOffset":123,"length":20}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":113,"line":113,"comment_lines":["[][113]"],"review_comment":["If I understand these changes, I think what\u0027s happening is that each key could appear in multiple samples, and together they should add up to the expected quantity?\r\n\r\nHave you considered scanning the samples to aggregate a summary of the _actual_ results, and then assert that this equals the _expected_ results? That is a more typical pattern for unit tests, and might be easier for others to follow, rather than a loop that interleaves mutating data structures with assertions.","That\u0027s true, it would be nicer, but has the downside of being more time consuming. \r\n\r\nToday we are reading samples and counting down till zero, so as soon as we have enough data (can be all in the first message), we good. Otherwise we keep listening for more data and check again until TIMEOUT.\r\nIf we aggregate and then check against expected, we will have first to wait until TIMEOUT, then check (sure we can have an assertBusy, but that is more or less the same, only with multiple timeouts).\r\n\r\nIn the worst scenario this is the same, but the test usually is quicker and pass as soon as we meet the criteria.","That said, all I did was minimal change to fix the test, and I have to say I also find the mutating data structures with assertions pattern very very strange.\r\nProbably it would be better to rewrite this test in a way similar to what you suggest (with assertBusy), favoring readability over speed, but I would leave it for a followup PR.","Oh I see what you mean... the test was already written using this mutable count-down-to-success style.\r\n\r\nMakes sense!"],"path":"test/external-modules/apm-integration/src/javaRestTest/java/org/elasticsearch/test/apmintegration/MetricsApmIT.java","id":35656,"created_at":"2024-10-28T16:13:14Z","original_position":77,"side":"RIGHT","position":77,"submitted_on_commit":"74fc1d25e3c46a59cdb2928f81eb63fb889dd955","diff_hunk":"@@ -91,21 +88,35 @@ public void testApmIntegration() throws Exception {\n                 var samples \u003d (Map\u003cString, Object\u003e) metricset.get(\"samples\");\n \n                 samples.forEach((key, value) -\u003e {\n-                    var assertion \u003d sampleAssertions.get(key);// sample name\n-                    if (assertion !\u003d null) {\n-                        logger.info(\"Matched {}\", key);\n+                    var valueAssertion \u003d valueAssertions.get(key);// sample name\n+                    if (valueAssertion !\u003d null) {\n+                        logger.info(\"Matched {}:{}\", key, value);\n                         var sampleObject \u003d (Map\u003cString, Object\u003e) value;\n-                        if (assertion.test(sampleObject)) {// sample object\n+                        if (valueAssertion.test(sampleObject)) {// sample object\n+                            logger.info(\"{} assertion PASSED\", key);\n+                            valueAssertions.remove(key);\n+                        } else {\n+                            logger.error(\"{} assertion FAILED\", key);\n+                        }\n+                    }\n+                    var histogramAssertion \u003d histogramAssertions.get(key);\n+                    if (histogramAssertion !\u003d null) {\n+                        logger.info(\"Matched {}:{}\", key, value);\n+                        var samplesObject \u003d (Map\u003cString, Object\u003e) value;\n+                        var counts \u003d ((Collection\u003cInteger\u003e) samplesObject.get(\"counts\")).stream().mapToInt(Integer::intValue).sum();\n+                        var remaining \u003d histogramAssertion - counts;\n+                        if (remaining \u003d\u003d 0) {\n                             logger.info(\"{} assertion PASSED\", key);\n-                            sampleAssertions.remove(key);\n+                            histogramAssertions.remove(key);\n                         } else {\n-                            logger.error(\"{} assertion FAILED: {}\", key, sampleObject.get(\"value\"));\n+                            logger.info(\"{} assertion PENDING: {} remaining\", key, remaining);\n+                            histogramAssertions.put(key, remaining);","submitted_line":113},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The variable name change from `sampleAssertions` to `valueAssertions` is clear but could be more descriptive. Consider renaming `valueAssertions` to something like `metricAssertions` or `sampleMetricAssertions` for better clarity.","nodes":[{"id":"test/external-modules/apm-integration/src/javaRestTest/java/org/elasticsearch/test/apmintegration/MetricsApmIT.java-test/external-modules/apm-integration/src/javaRestTest/java/org/ela